# Task 9: GitHub Branches Terminal Output
# This file contains the terminal output displaying the branch names and
# their status in the repository.

# NOTE: Replace with your actual terminal output after running the commands locally.

# Command to list local branches:
$ git branch
* main
  bug-fix-typo

# Command to list all branches (local and remote) with status:
$ git branch -a
* main
  bug-fix-typo
  remotes/origin/main
  remotes/origin/bug-fix-typo

# Explanation:
# - The asterisk (*) indicates the currently checked-out branch (main).
# - "main" is the default branch.
# - "bug-fix-typo" is the feature branch created for the typo fix.
# - remotes/origin/* are the remote-tracking branches on your fork.

# Alternative: View branches on GitHub via the web UI at:
